---
import UiShot from './UiShot.astro';
import NotifyFragment from './NotifyFragment.astro';
---
<section id="features" class="section features" data-snapshot="features" aria-labelledby="features-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">Features</p>
      <h2 id="features-title" class="display-lg">Built for the servers you already run</h2>
      <p>Containers, databases, NAS boxes and a few Raspberry Pis. Arkeep backs them up the same way and tells you when something is off.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="bento">
      <article class="card card--dark tile live" data-reveal>
        <div class="text">
          <h3 class="title-md">Know the moment it fails</h3>
          <p>Live progress while restic runs. Email, signed webhooks and Healthchecks.io pings on success or failure.</p>
        </div>
        <NotifyFragment />
      </article>

      <article class="card tile docker" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 70ms">
        <div class="text">
          <h3 class="title-md">Docker volumes, discovered</h3>
          <p>Arkeep lists containers and volumes on each host and follows them as services come and go.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ui-card" data-ui>
          <p class="ui-head">Add source <span>· web-01</span></p>
          <ul class="volumes">
            <li><span class="box checked" aria-hidden="true"></span>postgres_data<span class="meta">postgres:16</span></li>
            <li><span class="box checked" aria-hidden="true"></span>nextcloud_html<span class="meta">nextcloud:29</span></li>
            <li><span class="box" aria-hidden="true"></span>gitea_data<span class="meta">gitea:1.22</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card tile db" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 140ms">
        <div class="text">
          <h3 class="title-md">Databases straight into restic</h3>
          <p>Stream <code translate="no">pg_dump</code> or <code translate="no">mysqldump</code> with a command source. No temp files on disk.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ui-card" data-ui>
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>command</td><td><code translate="no">pg_dump -U app appdb</code></td></tr>
              <tr><td>directory</td><td><code translate="no">/etc/postgresql</code></td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card tile policy" data-reveal>
        <div class="text">
          <h3 class="title-md">One policy, many destinations</h3>
          <p>3-2-1 without scripts: a NAS, a bucket and an offsite box, each with its own retention.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="crop-dock"><UiShot name="ui-policy-destinations" alt="The Destinations card of an Arkeep policy, listing NAS (local) and Offsite copy in order" /></div>
      </article>

      <article class="card tile browse" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 70ms">
        <div class="text">
          <h3 class="title-md">Browse a snapshot, restore a file</h3>
          <p>Open any snapshot, walk its folders, download a file or a folder as ZIP, or restore a selection.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="crop-dock"><UiShot name="ui-snapshot-tree" alt="Arkeep snapshot browser showing the folders and files of a Postgres snapshot, with sizes" /></div>
      </article>

      <article class="card tile auth" data-reveal>
        <div class="text">
          <h3 class="title-md">Your login, your rules</h3>
          <p>Sign in with your identity provider, require two-factor for everyone, and give auditors read-only accounts.</p>
          <ul class="tags" aria-label="Supported">
            <li>OIDC</li><li>Keycloak</li><li>Authentik</li><li>Zitadel</li><li>TOTP 2FA</li><li>Read-only users</li><li>Audit log</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="crop-dock"><UiShot name="ui-2fa" alt="Arkeep profile setting to enable two-factor authentication" /></div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* Asymmetric bento: tiles differ in width and height so no row reads as three equal cards. */
  .bento {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(12, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--space-base);
    grid-template-areas:
      'live live live live live live live docker docker docker docker docker'
      'live live live live live live live db db db db db'
      'policy policy policy policy policy browse browse browse browse browse browse browse'
      'auth auth auth auth auth auth auth auth auth auth auth auth';
  }
  .live { grid-area: live; }
  .docker { grid-area: docker; }
  .db { grid-area: db; }
  .policy { grid-area: policy; }
  .browse { grid-area: browse; }
  .auth { grid-area: auth; }

  .tile { display: flex; flex-direction: column; overflow: hidden; min-width: 0; }
  .text { padding: var(--space-lg); display: grid; gap: var(--space-xs); align-content: start; }
  .text p { color: var(--body); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.55; max-width: 52ch; }
  .card--dark .text p { color: var(--on-dark-soft); }
  .text code { font-size: 0.88em; }

  /* Product fragments dock to the card's bottom-right edge and are cropped by it. */
  .crop-dock, .ui-card {
    margin: auto 0 0 var(--space-lg); background: var(--surface-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline-strong); border-right: 0; border-bottom: 0; border-top-left-radius: var(--radius-md); overflow: hidden;
  }
  /* GUI shots sit on the GUI's own page colour, inset like a window region. */
  .crop-dock { background: var(--canvas); padding: var(--space-base) 0 0 var(--space-base); }
  .ui-card { padding: var(--space-base) var(--space-md); font-size: 13px; display: grid; gap: var(--space-xs); background: var(--canvas-soft); }
  .ui-head { font-weight: 600; font-size: 13px; }
  .ui-head span { color: var(--body); font-weight: 400; }
  .volumes { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; }
  .volumes li { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--space-sm); padding: 8px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline); }
  .volumes .meta { margin-left: auto; color: var(--body); font-size: 12px; }
  .box { width: 14px; height: 14px; border: 1px solid var(--hairline-strong); border-radius: 4px; flex: none; background: var(--surface-card); }
  .box.checked { background: var(--brand); border-color: var(--brand); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 3px var(--surface-card); }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; }
  th { text-align: left; color: var(--body); font-weight: 500; font-size: 12px; padding-bottom: 4px; }
  td { padding: 8px var(--space-sm) 8px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline); white-space: nowrap; }
  td code { font-size: 12px; }

  .live .text { padding-bottom: var(--space-base); }

  .auth { flex-direction: row; align-items: stretch; }
  .auth .text { flex: 0 0 40%; padding-block: var(--space-xl); }
  .auth .crop-dock { flex: 1; margin: var(--space-xl) 0 0 0; align-self: flex-end; }
  .tags { list-style: none; margin: var(--space-sm) 0 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px; }
  .tags li { padding: 4px 10px; border-radius: var(--radius-pill); background: var(--hairline-soft); font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink); }

  @media (max-width: 1023px) {
    .bento {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      grid-template-areas: 'live live' 'docker db' 'policy browse' 'auth auth';
    }
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 1023px) {
    .live { flex-direction: row; }
    .live .text { flex: 0 0 38%; padding-bottom: var(--space-lg); }
    .live :global(.notify) { flex: 1; margin: var(--space-xl) 0 0 0; align-self: flex-end; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .bento { grid-template-columns: 1fr; grid-template-areas: 'live' 'docker' 'db' 'browse' 'policy' 'auth'; gap: var(--space-sm); }
    .auth { flex-direction: column; }
    .auth .text { padding-bottom: var(--space-lg); }
    .auth .crop-dock { display: none; }
    .text { padding: var(--space-md); }
    .crop-dock, .ui-card { margin-left: var(--space-md); }
  }
</style>
